  mattpocock/skills - Matt Pocock (MIT, (c) 2026 Matt Pocock). Under D31 this library
    keeps that repo's wording wherever the wording is what carries the value, so the
    files below hold passages in their author's expression and not only reimplemented
    patterns. The list is deliberately scoped by FILE, not by sentence: what a reader
    needs is which of our files to treat as carrying upstream text, and a sentence-level
    list is stale the day someone finds one more. Where a file is named here, assume its
    debt may run past the examples given.
      skills/review/standards-baseline.md, skills/review/SKILL.md,
        skills/review/reviewer-brief.md <- skills/engineering/code-review/SKILL.md.
        The Fowler smell baseline (entry wording, the what-it-is -> how-to-fix form, the
        "possible <smell>" framing), the two-axis "a change can pass one axis and fail
        the other" line, the repo-standard-overrides-the-baseline rule. The review
        chain, its channels, its dispatch and its gates are ours.
      skills/deploy-capability/SKILL.md rung 2 <- skills/engineering/wizard/SKILL.md.
        The static-trace rule for a generated operator script: do not run it end to end
        since it opens browsers and blocks on input, trace it statically, and the two
        things that trace checks. The payload fork itself, its counting test and the
        walkthrough machinery around it are ours.
      skills/writing-skills/SKILL.md <- .agents/writing-docs.md,
        skills/productivity/writing-for-agents/SKILL.md,
        skills/productivity/writing-great-skills/GLOSSARY.md (the pre-rename file),
        docs/productivity/wait-what.md. The branches-in-a-table rule, the
        environment-as-cache rule, the negation mechanism, the read-the-draft-for-its-
        silences rule, the fails-by-growing formulation and its four-hundred-line
        illustration. The bar's other rules, the frontmatter standard, the deletion test
        and the trap set around them are ours.
      docs/skills/README.md and the pages under docs/skills/ <- .agents/writing-docs.md,
        skills/productivity/writing-for-agents/SKILL.md. The four-section page spine
        (What it does / When to reach for it / Common questions / It's working if) and
        its orient-then-answer rationale, the working-if bar ("a few bullets naming what
        the reader sees when the skill is doing its job"), the compliance-check-wearing-
        this-section's-name line, the evidence-gated question sizing, and this file's own
        copies of the branches and cache rules. Every page's contents, and the
        bidirectional mapping the package gate enforces, are ours.
      skills/wait-what/SKILL.md, docs/skills/wait-what.md <-
        skills/productivity/wait-what/SKILL.md, docs/productivity/wait-what.md.
        The corrective's own framing, kept in its author's words: "the last message did
        not land", "comprehension failed here". The size gate, the context-line-leads
        rule, the routing table and the comms-block boundary are ours.
      skills/plan-grill/SKILL.md <- the grilling-question-format changeset that pinned
        the format into skills/productivity/grilling/SKILL.md, and
        skills/productivity/to-questionnaire/SKILL.md. The round's question format
        ("each question, then your recommendation on its own line - so the user answers
        by number") and the questionnaire unblock's rules (grill the user only about the
        send; most-important-first because async may get one pass; one idea per question
        with an answer stub under each). The two guards, the four-question cap, the
        one-way-door class, the front-door routing and the NEEDS_INPUT park are ours.
      docs/TRAPS.md trap 153 <- skills/productivity/to-questionnaire/SKILL.md. The
        "send, not the subject" antithesis, the "Markdown questionnaire aimed at the gap"
        phrasing, and the ordering-and-stub clause it restates. The trap's scenario and
        its Pass/Fail structure are ours.
      skills/codebase-audit/SKILL.md <- skills/engineering/improve-codebase-architecture;
        skills/orchestrating-agents/briefs-and-reviews.md <- skills/engineering/research;
        skills/groundwork/carving.md and skills/groundwork/SKILL.md <-
        skills/engineering/to-tickets (the slicing vocabulary, and the three-question
        gate on a proposed carve); skills/plan-grill/done-contract.md <-
        skills/engineering/to-spec. Short kept runs inside otherwise original
        procedures, found by the 2026-08-07 attribution sweep and listed here rather
        than paraphrased away.
      docs/DECISIONS.md and docs/TRAPS.md restate several of the rules above where a
        ruling or a trap turns on one. Those are records of what was adopted and name
        their source in the same breath; the reasoning and the scenarios are ours.

